WEBVTT

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:03.361
Imagine two boba clubs sell exactly the
same drink.

00:00:03.361 --> 00:00:04.730
Which deal costs less?

00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:08.256
You can answer by putting the two receipts
on one graph.

00:00:09.186 --> 00:00:11.416
Club A charges eight dollars to join.

00:00:11.416 --> 00:00:12.690
Club B charges two.

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:15.952
With zero drinks, those fees are already on
the receipts.

00:00:16.882 --> 00:00:20.487
Each new drink adds two dollars to A, but
four dollars to B.

00:00:20.897 --> 00:00:24.050
At one drink, A totals ten dollars and B
totals six.

00:00:24.980 --> 00:00:26.894
Move right one space for each drink.

00:00:26.894 --> 00:00:28.534
Move up for the total cost.

00:00:28.944 --> 00:00:30.995
A starts higher. B climbs more each time.

00:00:30.995 --> 00:00:33.047
Where do you think the lines will meet?

00:00:35.427 --> 00:00:38.206
At three drinks, both receipts say fourteen
dollars.

00:00:38.616 --> 00:00:40.315
Three tells you how many drinks.

00:00:40.315 --> 00:00:42.014
Fourteen tells you what you pay.

00:00:42.944 --> 00:00:44.537
Pause here and make a prediction.

00:00:44.537 --> 00:00:46.661
Which club costs less on the fourth drink?

00:00:48.521 --> 00:00:50.545
A costs sixteen. B costs eighteen.

00:00:50.545 --> 00:00:53.582
After the tie, the slower climb makes A
cheaper.
